# Byte Run (FLI)

# Each "line" of the image is compressed separately. This file
# represents one line.  For FLI files, the first byte means the packet count.

02         # packet count (relevant for FLI files, not FLC)

           # Packet 0 with negative byte count
FD         # $FD, unsigned, is -3. So, expect ABS(-3) bytes
AABBCC     # 3 bytes of data

           # Packet 1 with positive byte count
02         # $02, unsigned, is 2. So, repeat next byte 2 times
EE         # 1 byte of data, to be repeated
